WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Thread connects your thinking in Obsidian to Codex and MongoDB Atlas. We tested whether a harness can stop trusting an outdated memory and retain checked lessons.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The authored decision changes: a nonempty false string now means active. Thread invalidates the dependent historical procedure and excludes it from new context. That historical procedure was seeded.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
A real Codex experiment improves the fixed acceptance score from eleven to sixteen out of sixteen. A fresh review approves the work, and Atlas stores a reusable procedure.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Eighteen fresh sessions compare three context conditions. All conditions pass six out of six tasks. This fixture demonstrates no added procedural benefit; the shared corrected code already helps.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Twenty-four tests pass, and a fresh coordinator retrieves the Atlas evidence. Obsidian is installed and configured, but visual testing remains incomplete. This is an evidence replay, not live interaction.
